WEBVTT

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.260
Hurry!

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.600
Leave any cargo that isn't loaded!

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.560
Just get everyone aboard quickly!

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.010
Yes, sir!

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.100
Let none pass!

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.530
Just Munechika's men left?

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.330
Tusukuru's warships...

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.490
Not bad.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.680
Get Munechika's forces loaded up, on the double!

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.320
We're breaking through!

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.890
This <i>really</i> isn't looking good...

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:33.750
Munechika-sama!

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:36.850
Munechika, come on!

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.060
All of you, get to the ship as fast as you can. That's an order.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:46.960
But...

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.280
I said, that's an order!

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:50.860
Go!

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.250
I leave the princess in your care.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.250
If nothing else, for this very moment...

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.260
All forces, retreat!

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.880
Fall back!

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.180
To shield my companions,

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.010
a bloodthirsty demon shall I be, crushing all who oppose me!

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.570
Munechika!

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.210
What?

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:04.970
The Emperor...

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:08.670
It must be a mistake, right?

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.560
Everything is over.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:14.570
What of the capital? What of Yamato?

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:52.600
I still find it difficult to believe that the Emperor is dead.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.480
Yet the truth remains.

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:00.490
Our focus now ought to be on the future.

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.130
Am I wrong?

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.750
What <i>is</i> our future?

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.500
A foolish question, General Woshisu.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:20.620
Brother...

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:21.760
General Raikou...

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:23.050
General Dekoponpo...

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:23.760
I see you are safe.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.090
My Emperor!

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:35.230
I was so looking forward to sharing with you my glorious victories in Tusukuru...

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:30.230
You mean to say?

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.270
Is it not obvious?

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:37.610
The princess must become our new Empress.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.010
So it shall be.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.810
From this day onward, we guard the princess,

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:51.670
and offer our every aid in her ascension to Empress!

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.440
Oshutoru...

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.540
For that, without a doubt,
 would have been the Emperor's will!

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.200
Haku...

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.180
May I join you?

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:04.090
Sure.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.870
Munechika will be okay, right?

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:17.810
Of course.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:21.120
She wouldn't die so easily.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.450
You're right.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.950
It was a bit surprising, though.

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:32.680
What was?

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.260
The Emperor...

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.650
You seem more depressed than I thought you would.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.720
Depressed? Me?

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:45.170
Yeah.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:52.030
I can understand Nekone and the others, but you're not originally from Yamato.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.350
That's true.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:58.820
To be honest, I don't even know what I should think.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:04.040
The news of his death was just too sudden.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.100
<i>He appeared out of nowhere,</i>

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.970
<i>made a mess of everything,</i>

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.020
<i>and now he intends to vanish again?</i>

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:24.940
<i>Brother...</i>

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:34.730
Father...

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:44.760
Princess, please eat.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.710
No! I'm not hungry!

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:55.540
Father...

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:13.120
Don't leave me all alone...

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:23.040
Raise your head, Princess.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:25.130
Honoka...

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:29.130
Would the Emperor...

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:33.390
your father... wish to see you like this?

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.880
Thank you, Honoka.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:46.400
I don't know what my mother looked like,

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:49.900
but I'm sure she was a person like you.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.880
Princess...

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:53.880
Honoka-sama.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:56.740
What is it?

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.980
Oshutoru-sama is here.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.140
Oshutoru...

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:09.030
I've brought tea for the princess.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.740
I cannot guarantee its flavor, 
but by all means, please try it.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:20.070
Did you perhaps prepare it yourself, Oshutoru-sama?

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:21.060
Indeed.

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:28.060
I followed the steps as best I could, 
in hope it might help Her Highness feel better.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:30.320
I see.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.580
You made this tea for me.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.070
It's sure to be good.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.310
Princess!

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:24.650
Princess!

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:25.820
What is the matter!?

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.120
Th-The tea...

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.410
The princess drank some of the tea Oshutoru-sama brought her,

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.170
and then...

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:00.150
What's going on?

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:02.660
Oh, dear...

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:09.080
It's changed a lot in the short time we've been gone.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:14.540
Kuon...

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.120
Is that...

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:19.170
Yeah.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.850
It looks like it was true.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.020
The Emperor...

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.010
<i>Now, finally...</i>

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:34.610
<i>Someone can carry on my hopes.</i>

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.420
There's no time for this.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:40.620
Kuon...

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:43.070
We need to get back to the capital now.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:49.030
Yeah, you're right.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:02.080
I came when I heard the fuss, and what do I find?

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:06.600
You've really done it now,

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.170
Oshutoru.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.600
How about it?

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.260
Get on your knees and beg,

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:21.360
and I might just consider giving you a more comfortable cell.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:27.380
No one knows of my innocence better than I.

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:30.370
You may spare yourself the effort.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.570
You won't fool me.

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:40.210
You probably got close to the princess with that oh-so-loyal look on your face right now.

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:41.100
In that case...

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:46.510
This is a sign of my loyalty to the princess.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:51.940
F-Fine.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:54.180
I'll keep this safe.

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:58.560
You won't be needing it right now, anyway.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:03.910
Do whatever you must to make him confess his scheme.

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:04.660
Yes, sir.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:12.660
Poison?

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:13.910
Yes.

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:17.170
The herbalist tells me it's a powerful one.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.170
It rots away the throat and organs,

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:22.600
and dulls the mind.

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.550
How terrifying.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:30.260
The princess collapsed after drinking the tea Oshutoru brought her,

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:32.200
as I heard it.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:35.160
For crying out loud, that Oshutoru...

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.610
What a terrible thing he's done!

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.990
That's not funny.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:41.520
Him? The man most known for his loyalty?

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:42.530
I cannot believe it.

00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:46.160
No, he's extremely cunning.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:49.960
Unfortunately, given the present situation, we cannot say that for sure.

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:49.960
I never trusted him one bit.

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:50.830
What?

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.330
This was found in the room of General Oshutoru.

00:15:55.770 --> 00:16:02.120
I examined the contents, and it appears to be the same as the poison used on the princess.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.810
So it was General Oshutoru after all?

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:06.420
You see!?

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:07.590
How stupid.

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:08.970
I knew it! I knew it!

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:13.320
Indeed. There also exists the possibility that it was planted in an attempt to frame him.

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:19.950
And it's <i>equally</i> possible that he's simply attempting to make us think so.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:24.240
The princess does admire him a great deal.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:28.990
Looking back, is it possible that it was he who approached the princess?

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:34.810
Come to think of it, he originally came from the lesser lands of Ennakamui, didn't he?

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.490
Correct.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:40.720
If we assume he intends to take this opportunity to rebel...

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.490
What a bold plan.

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:43.770
Excuse me, Generals!

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.110
What is it?

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:47.810
We are in the middle of a meeting.

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:49.180
My deepest apologies.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.940
But this is an emergency!

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:54.270
What is it? Out with it.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:58.270
Oshutoru-sama's forces have swarmed the palace.

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:09.410
Withdraw your forces! Disperse at once!

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.160
Why must Oshutoru-sama be imprisoned?

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:13.120
That's right!

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:14.660
We refuse to accept this!

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:17.870
The General of the Right is under suspicion of treason.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:21.800
If you refuse to withdraw, 
you will be arrested as well!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:24.670
Oshutoru-sama would never rebel!

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:26.490
That's right!

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:29.880
No way in hell that would happen!

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:32.120
Oshutoru-sama would never betray Yamato!

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.210
Silence!

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.010
Foolish rabble.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:43.490
My, my... This is a problem.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.190
So what do we do?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.100
This is merely the beginning.

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:54.200
Even if we stop it this time, the feeling of unease in the capital will not disappear.

00:17:55.190 --> 00:18:00.930
We've lost the Emperor, and now the princess is at death's door.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:05.130
At this rate, Yamato might be torn apart from the inside out.

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:05.960
Huh?

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.820
Where are you going, General Vurai?

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:45.970
General Vurai...

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:53.130
So this is the end of the man I recognized as my equal.

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:32.150
What in the world?

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.820
Hurry, everyone!

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.970
That's right! We can't just let this happen!

00:20:58.970 --> 00:20:59.680
What's going on?

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:02.310
We must save Oshutoru-sama!

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:05.360
What... did he say?

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:06.810
Haku-san...

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:07.810
Brother!

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:10.800
Whoa, there.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:13.320
It's probably better not to do anything rash.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:15.030
Nekone-san!

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:16.460
But my brother...

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:24.370
It seems all did not settle with just the Emperor's death.

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:26.330
Yeah.

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:28.010
Ougi, Nosuri...

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.630
Can you find out for us?

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:32.080
Leave it to us.

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:37.220
Yakutowaruto, you take those two back to Hakuroukaku.

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:38.090
Gotcha.

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:38.920
No!

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:40.090
Please let me go!

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:43.650
I have to go to the palace and find out what's going on!

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:45.100
Neko-yan...

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.280
We got this, 'kay?

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:51.580
Might not seem like it, but we're princesses, y'know?

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:54.280
Right, Ruru-yan?

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:56.730
Huh? Y-Yeah!

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:59.330
Take care, you two.

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:02.450
From the looks of things, 
something strange is going on.

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:04.250
Don't worry.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:06.120
I'll go, too.

00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:09.970
Kuon and I will check out the city.

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:13.380
I'm counting on you all.

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:14.760
Yeah!

00:22:37.220 --> 00:22:38.470
What is this?

00:22:38.900 --> 00:22:40.640
What's going on?

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:44.250
Haku, look!

00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:55.500
Hear me!

00:22:55.920 --> 00:22:57.170
Just now,

00:22:57.170 --> 00:23:00.170
the fate of the imprisoned 
Oshutoru has been decided!

00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:10.980
By unanimous decision of the Eight Pillar Generals,

00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:14.230
at sunset tomorrow, Oshutoru, the General of the Right,

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:16.190
will be beheaded!

00:23:20.230 --> 00:23:20.940
Haku...
